# Git identity (tmwclaxton only)

This repository belongs to GitHub user **tmwclaxton** (`tmwclaxton/BumbleFriendsAuto`).

- Do **not** create commits with the `tobyclaxton` GitHub user or `toby.claxton@cineark.net`.
- Do **not** change global git config. Use this repo's local `user.name` / `user.email` (already set), or override a single commit with:

  `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME='Toby Claxton' GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL='57643714+tmwclaxton@users.noreply.github.com' GIT_COMMITTER_NAME='Toby Claxton' GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL='57643714+tmwclaxton@users.noreply.github.com'`

- Before `git push`, run `gh auth switch --user tmwclaxton`. If push returns 403 for `tobyclaxton`, switch and retry. After a successful push, switch back with `gh auth switch --user tobyclaxton` so other repos keep working.
- Do not amend or rewrite commits already on `origin` just to change author unless the user explicitly asks.
